{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvJyp35yZx2BLazRkJPB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No, not by itself. For Workers with a compatibility date of 2026-08-04 or later, Node.js compatibility is on by default. To turn it off, Cloudflare's docs say to add **both** `no_nodejs_compat` and `no_nodejs_compat_v2` to `compatibility_flags`, and to remove `nodejs_compat` or `nodejs_compat_v2` if they're there. Workers with an earlier compatibility date don't get Node.js APIs unless you add `nodejs_compat`, so you don't need an opt-out flag for those. This change is recent, so check the compatibility flags page before you depend on the exact cutoff date.\n\nSources:\n- [Compatibility flags · Cloudflare Workers docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/configuration/compatibility-flags/)\n- [Node.js compatibility is now enabled by default · Changelog](https://developers.cloudflare.com/changelog/post/2026-08-04-nodejs-compat-default/)\n- [Node.js compatibility · Cloudflare Workers docs](https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/runtime-apis/nodejs/)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1301,"cache_read_input_tokens":22456,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1301},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c3d22e95-a860-483c-becb-a38577155f35","uuid":"1ed06fb9-d6a5-4164-8ce1-f2dea606d87d","timestamp":"2026-10-11T10:42:46.712Z","request_id":"req_011CfvJyonTE7Ys899mzKtDr"}
